I have everything needed. Here is the complete picture of how owner CREATE (POST /owners) works.

## 1. The POST YAML (the create pipeline)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`
```yaml
composition:
  authorize: "hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')"

# Validate before Build so a missing or blank field is a 400 naming the offending
# fields, and the body is read (and republished) exactly once here.
validate:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.ValidateOwnerFields
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: build

build:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.BuildOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: save

save:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.SaveOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: respond

respond:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.RespondWithOwnerCreated
  govern: [ transaction ]
```

The pipeline is a 4-step chain: `validate → build → save → respond`, all under a `transaction` governance and gated by `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`.

## 2. The four Java function classes referenced by the YAML

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ValidateOwnerFields.java`
```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner;

import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

import net.officefloor.plugin.variable.Out;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto.OwnerFieldsDto;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RequestBody;

/**
 * Rejects a create-owner request that is missing or blank in any of firstName, lastName,
 * address, city or telephone, before {@link BuildOwner} runs. Runs first so an incomplete
 * body is a 400 naming the offending fields. Publishes the validated body for later steps.
 */
public class ValidateOwnerFields {

    public void service(@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto request, Out<OwnerFieldsDto> validated)
            throws MissingOwnerFieldsException {
        List<String> missing = new ArrayList<>();
        checkField("firstName", request.getFirstName(), missing);
        checkField("lastName", request.getLastName(), missing);
        checkField("address", request.getAddress(), missing);
        checkField("city", request.getCity(), missing);
        checkField("telephone", request.getTelephone(), missing);
        if (!missing.isEmpty()) {
            throw new MissingOwnerFieldsException(missing);
        }
        validated.set(request);
    }

    private static void checkField(String name, String value, List<String> missing) {
        if (value == null || value.isBlank()) {
            missing.add(name);
        }
    }
}
```

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java`
